  "notes": [
    "Preregistered interpretation: call full-lineage conflict reproducible only if both candidates are material and at least 3/4 folds per candidate are material. Standard10 underexposure requires below 15% of pool-opponent hands in both lineages. This is mechanism evidence only, not poker-strength evidence.",
    "Primary audit completed without updates. Both lineages: material conflict 4/4 folds and ordinary-vs-source-KL conflict 3/4 folds; Standard10 pool exposure ~20.8%, so the preregistered underexposure hypothesis is false.",
    "No Slumbot calls and no policy weights were changed. Full alpha_holdem suite passed 319/319."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Two frozen independent 1M integrated checkpoints reproduced material opponent-seat policy-gradient conflict in 4/4 deterministic folds each. Ordinary reward gradients also opposed the Standard10 forward-KL preservation gradient in 3/4 folds for both lineages. Standard10 received ~20.8% of pool hands and was the hardest fixed external anchor, rejecting simple underexposure as the primary mechanism.",
    "conclusion": "This is a concrete optimization failure, not evidence that the learned-policy family is exhausted or undertrained. The deployed coefficient-1 sum still harms one CFR4 seat group in each lineage, while group-only MGDA conflicts with source preservation. A seven-objective normalized minimum-norm direction over six anchor-seat reward losses plus Standard10 KL exists for both checkpoints with strictly positive worst alignment (+0.200/+0.186). Seat-only conflict did not independently meet its replication gate, so do not add a seat-specific architectural rule.",
    "decision": "ADMIT_SEVEN_OBJECTIVE_CONFLICT_AWARE_INTERVENTION_SMOKE",
    "next_step": "Run one separately preregistered matched offline update smoke from both 1M checkpoints on the frozen cohort, comparing the deployed ordinary PPO+KL direction against normalized seven-objective common descent with identical data, optimizer dose, and untouched multi-anchor/two-seat evaluation. If translation is broad and Standard10 preservation remains within gate, implement the minimal on-policy trainer contract before geometric scaling."
  },
